{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"bitumen-canophilic-pekingese","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\nThe infra/compose cohort contains audited comments or docstrings that obscure current behavior with repetition, obvious narration, duplicated explanation, or historical detail. The audit is pinned to `9e65567b79ffe872534c3c656ade7b34340d8192`.\n\n## Approach\nEdit explanatory text only in this directory/subsystem cohort. Condense it to current, non-obvious rationale and constraints; retain every file-specific preserve item and consumer contract below. Grouping adjacent files from one subsystem keeps the change reviewable in one session and permits one coherent verification pass without changing executable behavior.\n\n## Scope\n- `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml:1-24,81-136,160-234,250-322,332-408,431-548,570-574` — Preserve shutdown/drain bounds, persistent stores, credential/file mounts, Bedrock region variables, scratch-volume admission markers, loopback/proxy trust boundary, clone/write behavior, soft versus fail-closed secrets, non-destructive external volumes. Consumer: Docker Compose, deployment scripts, security/operators.\n- `infra/compose/Dockerfile.gerrit:1-17,34-42` — Preserve image purpose, required packages, exact g2p commit pin and why PyPI is unsuitable. Consumer: Docker builders/operators.\n- `infra/compose/Dockerfile.mcp:1-15,33-45,73-94,113-151` — Preserve locked build, runtime dependency boundary, non-root/runtime paths, real entrypoint requirement. Consumer: Docker builders/MCP operators.\n- `infra/compose/Dockerfile.opcert:1-13,33-41` — Preserve trusted gate image, agents dependency, non-root/runtime contract. Consumer: Docker builders/op-cert operators.\n- `infra/compose/Dockerfile.reviewbot:1-23,43-116,122-147` — Preserve runtime Git/scanner requirements, lock-based install, store helper, entrypoint and writable-path constraints. Consumer: Docker builders/review-bot operators.\n- `infra/compose/gerrit.config:1-10,70-77,99-121` — Preserve deployment location, OAuth boot prerequisites, topic-global collision warning, outbound mail disabled explicitly and restart required. Consumer: Gerrit/operators.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every listed location contains only current, non-obvious rationale or constraints after remediation; verified by reviewing the final diff against every Scope row.\n- [ ] Every preserve item and consumer contract in Scope remains explicit and accurate; verified by a row-by-row completion comment and the commands under Verification.\n- [ ] No executable behavior or test assertion changes; verified by the commands under Verification exiting 0.\n\n## Verification\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint`\n\nThe row-by-row diff review is authoritative for prose quality; the hygiene guard detects only its narrow deterministic history-token rule.","id":"a0f1-b86c-5199-4a42","parent_id":"49ac-d7e5-f383-4d7f","priority":3,"repos":["rebar"],"tags":["comments","documentation","maintainability","grouped-remediation"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Condense comments in infra/compose"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788570445871225746,"uuid":"ca6977b0-34d3-4206-a985-73831d7b015a"}